### OQ-030 — Live call events and result reconciliation [OPEN — Engineering, 2026-10-19]
D-58 needs, from the telecom partner: (1) **live** events during the call — leg 1 answered, leg 2 answered — for "Connecting to patient", "On call" and the transfer count; (2) a way for the backend to ask for call details when a result is late, before the app shows "Result not received"; (3) the mapping of each vendor's codes (Ozonetel `CustomerStatus`, Knowlarity hangup causes) to D-58's buckets, per leg; (4) how a failed HA transfer leg is reported. Without (1), "Connecting" disappears and transfer cases can't be counted.

**Update 2026-10-23 (D-58 point 14):** requirement — the app shows the call's status within about 5 seconds of the partner reporting it; Engineering chooses polling or push. Also needed: a backend check "is this call valid" (gate time since `customerAnswered`, call live) before Confirm & transfer shows; measure from today's logs the usual result delay (sets the wait) and a maximum call length. Which partner handles Cat4 / Non-Value Meds, and whether it sends live events, is still to confirm. Ozonetel reference: `reference/telephony/ozonetel-webhook-reference.md`.

**Update 2026-10-24:** method decided — polling, in both the web portal and the app (D-58 point 19). Remaining for Engineering: interval, maximum call length, result-wait time.

**Update 2026-10-24:** confirm that Ozonetel reports who ended a non-transfer call (`doctorAnswered` HANGUP/DIAL or CDR `Comments`) in time for state 16 — the reference says yes; Apurva has seen hang-up mainly during transfers.

### OQ-031 — Mobile data during a normal call [OPEN — Engineering, 2026-10-19]
On phones without VoLTE, mobile data pauses during a normal call, so the app can't count or send Confirm & transfer. Agreed for now (D-58): the case goes as a forward; track how often it happens. Engineering: can the app detect data loss during a call?

### OQ-032 — HA reservation and allocation [OPEN — Apurva + Engineering + Ops, 2026-10-24]
Target design (D-58 point 15, option A) needs an HA reserved at the start of the doctor's call, so the route (transfer / forward) is known before Confirm. Today HAs click Assign and wait 60 s for a live transfer, else get a failed-transfer order — about 35% of single-call cases end as two calls, and failed-transfer callback TAT suffers. Apurva is relooking at HA allocation separately (outside this project); until reservation exists, the fallback (option B) applies.

### OQ-033 — Ops review for calls without a record [CLOSED — D-83, 2026-11-03: no Ops queue; no record after the wait time (setting) → prescription not confirmed, case back through hold and retry, no ₹20, mismatch logged] [was PROVISIONALLY DECIDED — D-73, 2026-10-29: 30-minute configurable cut-off approved; SOP, monitoring and earnings provisional] [was OPEN — Apurva + Ops, 2026-10-24]
D-58 point 20 depends on Ops. To lock: (1) a review queue for "Prescription submitted" cases whose call record **never arrives** (after how long?); (2) what Ops does with each — confirm, cancel, or callback — and who tells the patient; (3) the flag and per-doctor metric for Unavailable and for submitted-without-record (thresholds, SOP, who acts); (4) whether doctor earnings count only after confirmation. Lock before the doctor app goes live.
**Separate discussion (Apurva, 2026-10-24):** what happens when a submitted case's record arrives late showing **under 50 s or no answer** — not part of this review queue; to be decided on its own (relates to the 50-second rule across dropped calls).

### OQ-034 — Icons on buttons: one rule [ANSWERED — RULES §9.1, 2026-10-24; no screen changes needed] [was OPEN — Apurva, 2026-10-24; do before the final render]
Buttons are inconsistent today: Call patient / Call again (phone), Callback (calendar), Skip HA (track-next), Unavailable (phone-off), Request next case (arrow after) have icons; Confirm prescription / transfer / forward, Back to Home, Yes still talking / No call ended, Release case, Stay on this case have none. Needs one design-system rule (RULES §9.1) and a pass over every screen — ideally before the terminal's final render so screens aren't rendered twice.

### OQ-035 — Orders with no medicines [OPEN — Engineering + Ops, 2026-11-01, D-80]
Keep orders with no medicines out of the doctor queue and send them to Ops. If one reaches a doctor, the app offers only Release case, and the released case goes to Ops (not back to the queue). Engineering: how an empty order is detected at assignment; Ops: who handles them and what happens to the order.

### OQ-036 — Phone can't do faster sign-in at the moment of Turn on [CLOSED — D-93, 2026-11-09: neutral notice + Continue → Home] [was OPEN — Apurva, 2026-11-09]
On the faster sign-in offer, the phone can answer "unavailable" when the doctor taps Turn on, for example because fingerprints were removed after the offer appeared. app-logic §2 lists only enabled / cancelled / failed / offline. `[OPEN DECISION]` placeholder in the build (step 1, session 3): treated as a failed turn-on ("Couldn't turn on faster sign-in." · Try again · Not now). Panel value: Faster sign-in offer = `unavailable`.

### OQ-037 — Prototype stand-ins from run A1 [MOCK ASSUMPTION — accepted by the main thread, 2026-11-09; prototype only]
For the prototype, not product rules: a case opened directly (`?s=` / Jump) starts 30 minutes of availability if none is set; Set availability / Add time fail only when offline (the story has no server-failure value for them); the drawn text and decimal keyboards appear only in capture mode (desktop review types with the computer keyboard); the Rx viewer's 300 ms double-tap window and the 4 s toast are interaction constants (`UI_TIMING`), not panel settings; "Request next case" = back to Home and request at once. Source: `docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/run-A1/REPORT.md`.

### OQ-038 — Prototype stand-ins from run B (Pilot, Fallback B) [MOCK ASSUMPTION — accepted by the main thread, 2026-11-10; prototype only]
For the prototype, not product rules: 14 Transferred counts the prescription at once (one transfer event), forwards (B3 / 15 / 16 / Pilot 7d) only on the partner's result (CW-F2); the `pilot_no_ha_free` scenario reads the simulator's HA "free" as none; a failed transfer request from B2 goes 13 → 15; a call that ends during B2 / 13 → 16, nothing counted; B3 / 15 wait for the hang-up only (the result also counts as the hang-up); on the live B1 the 7b question still comes after the no-result timeout; B1 Confirm prescription goes straight to B2 (confirm-failed / busy story answers apply to post-call confirms only); story "Pending blocks confirm" on a case with nothing Pending puts its last medicine back to Pending; 13 keeps the neutral script (D-102); a Fallback B picture opened with a story case without an HA call uses the picture's Pilot case. Setting `pilotTalkAfterGate` 60 s (stand-in). Source: `docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/run-B/REPORT.md`.
### D-61 · Entry screens: logo, OTP Back, unlock buttons, faster sign-in offer — 2026-10-25
- **Decision (Apurva):**
  1. **Logo on every screen except the case page and task overlays** — on sign-in, OTP (all states), returning unlock, the faster sign-in offer and Home; not on the case page, Prescribe, bottom sheets, the Rx viewer or other full-screen task overlays. **Replaces D-42's "logo only on home-base screens".** D-42's space reason no longer holds: the faster sign-in card moved off OTP (D-44/D-45) and OTP loses its header Back. Check during the render: OTP with the keyboard open at 360 still shows the code boxes, the error line and Verify; if not, back to Apurva.
  2. **OTP has no header Back** — "Change" next to the number and the phone's back gesture cover it; the "Back" text label beside the arrow was also inconsistent with the rest of the app.
  3. **Returning unlock: "Use OTP instead" becomes a quiet button** (it is a fallback, not a real alternative), matching the faster sign-in offer's "Not now". Order: Unlock with fingerprint (primary) · Use OTP instead (quiet) · Not you? Switch account.
  4. **Faster sign-in offer:** add the missing states — enabling failed (notice; try again or Not now), prompt cancelled by the doctor (back to the offer, no error), no fingerprint/face set up on the phone (don't offer it, or point to phone settings — to agree in the screen pass), offline. **Hero icon placement aligned with returning unlock** (same tile, same place on both sibling screens).
- **Why:** sibling screens should look and behave alike; one control per action; error states are part of done.
- **Rejected:** keeping D-42's logo rule (space argument outdated); logo on the case page (patient context needs the space); "Use OTP instead" as an outlined secondary (competes with the main action).
- **Next:** a full pass over all approved screens against the standards checklist plus these points, findings to Apurva before any render.

### D-62 · Outcome cards tinted; 7b stays neutral; no overlay on closed cases — 2026-10-25
- **Decision (Apurva):** (1) **Status cards are tinted by outcome** — success (light green: confirmed, transferred, forwarded), neutral (light grey: prescription submitted, patient unavailable), warning (amber: Health Advisor unavailable). Plain white outcome cards looked like content and were easy to miss; the tint also separates the result from the small green "Prescribed" tags. Design system: `.tm-status-card--success / --neutral / --warning` [PROPOSED], RULES §9.3, beyond-salt.md. Affects approved closed screens (`e-*`) — re-rendered in the full screen pass. (2) **7b "Are you still on the call?" stays neutral** (amber only for problems); its notice must not look like an input field — fix in the screen pass. (3) **No grey overlay behind a closed case** — content stays readable, shown read-only and muted (rebuild item: View Rx, medicines, notes read-only).
- **Rejected:** amber for 7b (dilutes amber); overlay on closed cases (modal metaphor; doctor may review what was prescribed).
- **Update 2026-10-25 (Apurva, after a one-screen experiment — `docs/renders/2026-10-25-card-tray-experiment/`):** (4) **Card look = C5**: tint + 1px edge in the tone colour, no drop shadow. Neutral keeps a **grey-100 fill** with a grey-200 edge (grey-50 is the page colour; grey-200 reads disabled). Rejected: tint only (success too pale on the grey page), left accent bar (weak, bends at the corner), border only (looks like a selected field — same problem as 7b), white card with icon chip (looks like content). (5) **Bottom action bar = T3**: hairline top edge + soft upward shadow; SALT's shadow points down, so the bar merged with white cards. Rejected: upward shadow only (soft), grey bar (reads disabled, buttons compete). (6) 7b question shown as plain text, no box. (8) **Tray depth = option B** (Apurva, 2026-10-26): same hairline and shape, deeper upward shadow (0 -8px 24px, 10%). Rejected: side shadows (a full-width bar has no sides to cast from), floating bar with margins (breaks the 7b pair at 360, content shows around it, reads as a half-open sheet), square corners (no gain). `exp-tray-shape-w360.png`. (7) **B3 is amber, like 15** (Apurva, 2026-10-26): same outcome and same action for the doctor (forwarded, read the script, end the call); amber = done but you still have to act. Replaces the earlier green. Research: Polaris / Atlassian / Material 3 tint + icon for status; iOS / Material bars use an edge or upward shadow.

### D-63 · Request next case checks the call has ended (15, B3) — 2026-10-25
- **Decision (Apurva):** on the two closed screens where the doctor is still on the line — **15** (transfer failed) and **B3** (forwarded, no Health Advisor free) — tapping **Request next case** asks the backend whether the call has finished (Ozonetel `callFinished`). Finished → the next case loads. Still live → nothing loads; a line in the action bar: "End the call to get your next case." The button stays enabled (the doctor learns why on tap). Back to Home stays available.
- **Why only these two:** Cat4 and Non-Value Meds unlock Confirm only after the call result arrives, i.e. after the call has ended (app-logic §4); in a successful transfer (14) the doctor leaves the call. Both 15 and B3 are Ozonetel flows, so the live/finished signal exists — no Knowlarity "unknown" case.
### D-101 · Hand-off kit Product answers for Sign-in (o04–o26) — 2026-11-09
- **Decision (Apurva, on the main thread's recommendations):** (o04) more than 10 digits that aren't a +91 / 0 prefix → show "That’s more than 10 digits. Check the number." instead of cutting silently. (o05) no passive offline notice on Sign-in; the notice shows only after Send OTP. (o07) the logo's 16 from the top is measured from the **safe area** (below the status bar / notch). (o08) Android back on Sign-in (the first screen) **leaves the app**. (o10) coming back from OTP via Change keeps the number and it edits normally (the first typed digit does **not** replace it). (o11) Terms → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/terms-and-conditions`, Privacy → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/privacy-policy` (placeholders, linked from the live Terms page), configurable from the server, not typed into the app. (o17) Sign up opens a browser **inside the app** (with a close button). (o18) nothing is remembered per number; an earlier answer shows again only after a new Send OTP. (o25) "New to Truemeds? Sign up" becomes one copy entry with a `{link}` placeholder. (o26) "Call Doctor Ops" on a device that can't call → open WhatsApp to the same number; without WhatsApp, show the number with a copy button.
- **Amended same day (Apurva):** the kit is a hand-off of a **prototype with a fake backend**, so the Backend and Design items (o01, o02, o03, o12, o15, o16, o19, o21, o22, o24) are not left open either: each becomes DECIDED with **the prototype's own mock value or behaviour**, marked `[MOCK]` and "keep configurable" so nobody treats it as a production promise. o23 (Expo or plain React Native, navigation library) is the app team's choice and is stated as theirs, not as an open question. o09 stays a prototype-only note.
- **Why:** platform norms (Android back, safe area, in-app browser); a silent cut can hide a wrong digit; Change usually fixes one digit; one copy entry translates safely; the server stays the truth for attempts.
- **Rejected:** keeping the current build's assumptions for o04, o08 and o10.
- **Applied by:** the sign-in follow-up run (`docs/renders/2026-11-09-signin-d101/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md`) for o04, o10, o11, o25 in the prototype; the kit run moves all ten to DECIDED. o07, o08, o17, o26 are native-only (the web prototype has no status bar, app back, in-app browser or call capability).

### D-102 · Launch B: Transferring… (13) keeps the neutral script — 2026-11-10
- **Ruling (main thread, inside D-83 / D-85; run B review):** in launch B (Fallback B), 13 Transferring… keeps the neutral Pilot script `call.scriptNeutral`; `call.scriptTransfer` ("Please stay on the line…") is version A only (app-logic §4 script list; §5 "Transfer path in B reuses 13–15"). The approved `t13-connecting-ha` picture at 390 shows the version-A script and is re-rendered from the build (backlog §2l).
- **Why:** the build follows app-logic; the picture predates the Fallback B launch decision.

### D-103 · Hand-off kit viewer redesign and in-site downloads — 2026-11-10
- **Decision (Apurva, after reviewing a working preview):** the viewer is cut down to what helps an engineer build or helps Apurva walk them through it. Screens get a tab per screen, the phone fixed on the left and a right panel with "When this shows" (plain words) and the tapped element's details; Building blocks get "Where it's used" across screens, linked both ways; internal labels and section numbers go; duplicate tables and the extra pictures go; downloads (whole kit zip and key single files) live inside the site, not Google Drive. Proposal: `docs/proposals/2026-11-10-kit-viewer-cleanup.md`; reference: `docs/renders/2026-11-10-kit-cleanup/preview/`.
- **Why:** the pilot viewer overwhelmed on first open; an outside team can't use our internal codes; in-site downloads always match the viewer's version, Drive would fall behind and need per-person sharing.
- **Rejected:** a separate "components" tab (Building blocks already is that; it gains "Where it's used" instead); keeping the 360 picture (the 360 limit is stated instead); a "Behaviour" list of decision numbers per element (replaced by answered questions in plain words, once per state); Google Drive for downloads.

### D-104 · Faster sign-in offer: again at each OTP sign-in, at most 3 times — 2026-11-10
- **Decision (Apurva):** after "Not now" (or the phone's back gesture), the faster sign-in offer comes back at the doctor's next OTP sign-in, and the next, until faster sign-in is turned on — **at most 3 times in total** (a Product setting, starting value 3). After that it isn't shown again; Profile still turns it on. "Not available on this phone" counts as shown. Remembered per phone and mobile number, as today. Closes OQ-023; replaces D-45's "offered once".
- **Why:** the point is cutting SMS cost, and every OTP sign-in is an SMS sent — the right moment to ask again. Doctors stay signed in between sessions, so OTP sign-ins are rare and the re-ask isn't frequent; the cap stops nagging a doctor who has decided no.
- **Rejected:** never re-offering (placeholder; loses the SMS saving); offering at every app open (nags); no cap.

### D-105 · Returning unlock: two buttons; Use OTP opens sign-in with the number filled in — 2026-11-10
- **Decision (Apurva):** returning unlock drops "Not you? Switch account". It keeps **Unlock** (primary) and **Use OTP instead** (quiet). Use OTP instead, and the automatic fallback after 3 failed unlocks, open **Sign-in with the remembered number filled in** — no SMS until the doctor taps Send OTP. To change account, the doctor edits the number there. Sign-in reached this way follows the normal Sign-in rules: no Back button; the phone's back gesture leaves the app (D-101); reopening the app shows unlock again. Amends D-61 point 3.
- **Why:** three stacked buttons with two quiet ones looked odd; Switch account and Use OTP instead both led to sign-in, so one control now does both. Not sending the SMS straight away also avoids an SMS when the doctor only wanted to switch account.
- **Rejected:** keeping Switch account; a special back gesture from this Sign-in to unlock (rare mistake; reopening the app already returns to unlock; one Sign-in behaving differently is harder to build and explain).

